<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-1076] Set hbase.client.retries.number for JDBC</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-1076</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;If a user has &quot;org.apache.phoenix:phoenix-core:4.x.x&quot; jar added as a dependency in JDBC interpreter, and for some reason phoenix was not accessible or not properly configured; then the phoenix tries to for 35 times (which is default for hbase.client.retries.number) and each retires is 8 second apart, before it finally fails.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
